edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186533637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186533637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533962 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533986 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533986 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269383" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533986 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533986 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26793c1a-40f5-5bd2-9877-7d31b77eb2ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533986 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5\\end{aligned}])=3([\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 15\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 30 \\\\ -3 & -15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-265777" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533992 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533992 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=(det(X))^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35662c2c-d0a2-5e1c-b319-cae7bd255ca0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533992 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=(det(X))^{2}=({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{22} & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{21}) \\\\ 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{12}) & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2det(X)[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=2(4\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 & -42 \\\\ 14 & 56\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533993 #edb/ref 1069 "q-265773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533993 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533993 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X)).\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533993 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "378ecb1a-5423-57cf-9a92-70fe30005016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533993 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X))=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}_{22}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{{x}_{21}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{12}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{-{x}_{11}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{-4-(-3)} & \\frac{1}{-4-(-3)} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-4-(-3)} & -\\frac{(-1)}{-4-(-3)}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{-1} & \\frac{1}{-1} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-1} & -\\frac{(-1)}{-1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534000 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534000 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269374" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534000 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534000 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)={y}^{T}Ax$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534000 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "46d18a08-f2dc-5cb8-81b8-c0b6c16aa5ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534000 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry